WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.600
Speaker 1: Let's start today with a positive story&nbsp;
that reminds us that sometimes sometimes activism&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:14.320
and media pressure can actually have an effect.&nbsp;
Nancy Pelosi, the Democratic speaker of the House,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:22.720
has done a complete 180, and she is now supporting&nbsp;
a ban on members of Congress trading individual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:27.840
stocks. Now, this doesn't mean it's actually&nbsp;
going to happen. It doesn't mean it's actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:34.080
going to pass. It may. We'll have to wait and&nbsp;
see. But in just two short months, Nancy Pelosi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:41.360
not because she wants to, but because she was&nbsp;
embarrassed and pressured into it, has done a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:46.320
complete 180 and has gone from. There's no reason&nbsp;
members of Congress should be banned from trading&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:54.080
individual stocks to I'd be open to it too. Let's&nbsp;
actually go ahead and do it. So as a reminder,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:59.680
back in December of last year, just two&nbsp;
months ago, Nancy Pelosi was asked about this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:04.960
and she rejected the idea of a stock trading&nbsp;
ban for members of Congress. Here's that clip.&nbsp;

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:09.680
Speaker 2: You should members of Congress and&nbsp;
their spouses be banned from trading in individual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:13.440
stocks while serving in Congress?
Speaker 3: No, I don't know to this second one.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:22.000
We have a responsibility to report in the stock&nbsp;
on stuff, but I don't. I'm not familiar with that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:28.000
five month review. But if people&nbsp;
aren't reporting, they should be. Yeah,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:34.720
because this is a free market and people&nbsp;
and we have a free market economy that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:39.360
should be able to participate in that.
Speaker 1: So that was up in December. Then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:47.120
we got to January and in January, Nancy Pelosi&nbsp;
said, Well, I'm open to a stock trading ban&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:52.400
from Congress. I have great confidence in the&nbsp;
integrity of my members. They are remarkable.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:58.560
So when people talk about, well, somebody might&nbsp;
do this and somebody I trust our members to give&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:02.800
a blanket attitude of, we can't do this and we&nbsp;
can't do that because we can't be trusted. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:09.360
don't buy into that. But if members want to do it,&nbsp;
I'm OK with that. And then the latest news is that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:17.280
Nancy Pelosi is now pushing a stock trading&nbsp;
ban for members of Congress Axios reporting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:24.480
just hours ago. House Speaker Nancy Pelosi is&nbsp;
moving to ban stock trading on Capitol Hill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:31.440
after having consistently opposed such a measure.&nbsp;
This adds unprecedented momentum to an issue that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:37.840
also has bipartisan support on the Senate side.&nbsp;
Pelosi's in premature follows building momentum&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:42.960
in both parties. Some progressive Democrats&nbsp;
and MAGA Republicans have united on a proposal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:47.840
to ban sitting lawmakers from trading&nbsp;
individual stocks. Pelosi, who expressed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:52.640
opposition in the past and some other Democratic&nbsp;
leaders, have been slow to take up the issue,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.440 --> 00:03:00.960
despite reported interest from House Minority&nbsp;
Leader Kevin McCarthy. So now the idea, as Axios&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:08.320
says, is amend the Stock Act from 2012, which&nbsp;
governs how members disclose purchase and sale&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:16.320
of stocks to eliminate the trading of individual&nbsp;
stocks by members of Congress. This is very, very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:22.560
interesting now. This doesn't mean it will happen,&nbsp;
but this is without a doubt the most momentum&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:27.760
we've seen in this direction, and I think it&nbsp;
has to be restated again and again. Nancy Pelosi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:35.920
doesn't want to do this. Nancy Pelosi notoriously&nbsp;
is involved in individual stock trading options&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:42.080
put. I mean, it's been widely reported. She&nbsp;
doesn't want this, but it is because of pressure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:48.880
and essentially being embarrassed into having&nbsp;
to be open to it that it has gained momentum and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:55.680
that's something we all did and some media outlets&nbsp;
have been doing. Now this is not going to be,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.480 --> 00:04:01.840
you know, it's not. There are some who are&nbsp;
opposing this on the basis that it's some kind of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:10.160
oppressive, authoritarian, you know, whatever,&nbsp;
if you choose to run for the House or Senate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:16.800
and you know, if I do that, I won't be able to&nbsp;
trade individual stocks. I can tell I can still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:23.840
hold mutual funds. I can still own the stocks&nbsp;
and put them in a blind trust. This is not super&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:27.840
oppressive, guys, and it does make perfect&nbsp;
sense because not only are you in a position&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:35.760
to know ahead of time about events that could&nbsp;
impact stock prices the way we saw happen in that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:41.200
crazy couple week period at the start of the&nbsp;
pandemic, and we saw Senator Kelly Loeffler&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:44.640
and others dumping stocks and buying&nbsp;
stocks and all these different things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:52.080
on the basis of of what they presumably logically&nbsp;
were told at some of these pre-COVID briefings.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:58.240
It's not just that you learn about things ahead&nbsp;
of time, it's also that your decisions can impact.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:05.280
The prices of stocks now, I think if we really&nbsp;
want to be thorough, it's important to say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:12.640
even without trading stocks. If at the time&nbsp;
that you become a member of the House or Senate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:18.400
you know what stocks you own, even if you can't&nbsp;
trade them, you can still try to legislate in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:26.560
ways that would be advantageous to you. Right. So&nbsp;
imagine I enter the house and I know that I own. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:31.600
don't know a bunch of stocks of a bunch of shares&nbsp;
of Google just to make it very, very simple.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:40.640
Even if I can't trade those while I am in the&nbsp;
House or Senate, I could still push legislation or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:46.720
vote in a way that would bolster the value of the&nbsp;
Google stock I know I have without trading it. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:52.320
even this, which some are saying, Oh, it's too, or&nbsp;
it's too much too authoritarian, it's too crazy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:59.360
it still leaves itself open to sort of abuse and&nbsp;
manipulation due to the power that legislators&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:04.000
have. But it would be a big deal. It would be a&nbsp;
big deal. And so we're going to follow whether&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:09.280
it actually happens. It really makes perfect&nbsp;
sense. Many members of the House and Senate are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:14.080
in favor of it. And the truth is, I hate to say&nbsp;
this, but some of them are in favor of it because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:17.280
they know that there's still a bunch of ways&nbsp;
around it that they're going to be able to find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:24.880
it. It's not just because they think it's the&nbsp;
right thing to do, and it's not just because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:28.320
they would get the benefit of optics. It's&nbsp;
also because many of them have a number of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:33.840
different ways around it, and the devil will be&nbsp;
in the details. How is it worded with regard to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:38.480
blind trusts? How is it worded with regard to&nbsp;
mutual funds? How is it worded with regard to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:42.880
the spouses or family members of those&nbsp;
in the House and Senate? You know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:48.880
Nancy Pelosi's husband has been a big element&nbsp;
of focus when it comes to her stock trading. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:56.800
many details to be sorted out. But it is a very&nbsp;
it's a welcome 180 from just two months ago.

